          <span data-i18n="changelogTitle">{t(locale, 'changelogTitle')}</span>
          <span class="changelog-badge">v1.21.0</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.21.0 — 2026-08-13</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>A wrong address no longer just shows the homepage</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Mistype a URL or follow an old link and you landed <strong>silently on the homepage</strong> — the site even told your browser everything was fine. That included pages that really had existed: team pages change at every June season rollover, so every link to a retired team quietly led to the homepage. There is now a proper <strong>“page not found”</strong> page pointing to volleyball, basketball, home and contact</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>The club crest is the club crest again</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The little icon in the browser tab had, since day one, been the <strong>logo of the development tool</strong> the site was built with, not the KSCW crest. It is now the crest — and also an app icon for “add to home screen”</li>
              <li>Sharing a kscw.ch link on <strong>WhatsApp, Instagram or Facebook</strong> produced a <strong>blank grey tile</strong>. It now shows the club crest as a preview image</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>The privacy policy is accurate again</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The imprint and privacy policy named <strong>Hetzner</strong> as the website host. The site runs on <strong>Cloudflare</strong> — so a data-access request would have gone to a company holding nothing about you. Corrected; Hetzner stays, correctly described as the home of the club database</li>
              <li>Newly described: the <strong>form spam protection</strong>, the <strong>newsletter</strong>, and <strong>club registration</strong> — the last of which collects an AHV number, payment details and sometimes an identity document, and was not mentioned in the policy at all</li>
              <li>The cookie section described cookies that do not exist. The site sets <strong>no cookies</strong> and uses <strong>no analytics</strong>; it stores only your colour scheme, language and roster view. That is why it needs <strong>no cookie banner</strong> — which the policy now says plainly. It also carries a date now</li>
              <li><strong>Instagram feeds</strong> on team pages loaded immediately, even though the privacy policy explicitly promised the opposite. They now load only after you agree</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Team pages finally say when and where the team trains</h3>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Training times, weekday and venue</strong> are now in the page itself instead of appearing after loading. The data was always there — it was simply discarded. This is the most asked question on the whole site</li>
              <li>On Google all 16 team pages were titled just “<strong>D1 — KSC Wiedikon</strong>” with no description. They now carry the full team name, the sport and the league</li>
              <li>Basketball leagues showed as <strong>federation codes</strong> (“H3LS”, “D1LRA”). They now read “3. Liga” and “1. Liga”</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Membership: no more contradictory instructions</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The page said you get a <strong>paper registration form</strong> from your coach — twenty lines above four buttons linking to the working online form. It now describes what actually happens</li>
              <li>The <strong>CHF 100 surcharge</strong> for an unfulfilled officials duty in basketball was written and translated but <strong>displayed on no page</strong>. Someone budgeting CHF 520 could be invoiced CHF 620. It is now shown with the fees</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Small things that were bigger than they sound</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>After a <strong>failed submit</strong> of the contact or feedback form, every retry was doomed — the spam protection issues its check code only once. The second attempt now works</li>
              <li>The <strong>contact form ran off the right edge on phones</strong> — exactly where a prospective member is meant to take the first step</li>
              <li><strong>Printing</strong> a page produced a near-blank sheet: white text on white paper. Anyone printing hall addresses for a noticeboard now gets something readable</li>
              <li>In the dark theme, <strong>fixture times, news dates and table headers</strong> were too faint; in the light theme two libero shirt numbers were <strong>white on white</strong></li>
              <li>The homepage now has a <strong>trial-session button</strong> — previously nothing on it led to joining. The subtitle now names <strong>Zürich-Wiedikon</strong></li>
              <li>The team count was stated <strong>three different ways</strong>. Now consistent. There is also a <strong>sitemap.xml</strong> for search engines</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.20.0 — 2026-08-12</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>The page no longer loads in German and then jumps to English</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Reading the site in <strong>English</strong> meant seeing the <strong>finished German page</strong> first and the translation only afterwards. Not the split second it looks like on a fast connection: measured at <strong>1.7 to 2.7 seconds</strong> on a normal mobile link. On the home page the German version is now not visible in a single frame; elsewhere about 0.25 seconds remain</li>
              <li>The cause was ordering, not speed: the translation file was not requested until the <strong>whole page</strong> had loaded — including a 398 KB icon bundle. It is now the very first thing requested</li>
              <li>Three texts were <strong>permanently</strong> wrong rather than briefly: this Feedback page said "WAS IST NEU" above the English changelog, and the home page's game tables stayed German in every language ("Laden…", "Keine Spiele gefunden.")</li>
              <li>"<strong>No news available.</strong>" appeared on the home page and on News while the news was still loading — a claim nobody could know at that moment. It now shows only when there genuinely is none</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
