            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.19.0 — 2026-08-12</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Every youth team now states which birth years can play</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>Every youth card carries a <strong>birth-years line</strong> — basketball U18 "Birth years: 2009, 2010" down to U8 "Birth years: 2019, 2020". The first question a parent asks was not answered anywhere on the site</li>
              <li>The line <strong>moves on by itself</strong>: on <strong>1 August</strong> every category shifts by a year, and it does so even if the site is not rebuilt at that moment. Nobody has to keep it up to date</li>
              <li>The <strong>U18 girls read 2009–2012</strong>, because there is no U16 girls' team this season and the two U18 squads carry those years as well. That is not a fact about U18 but about this season's roster — the line reads the roster from Directus, so it narrows again by itself once there is a U16 girls' team</li>
              <li><strong>Volleyball draws the line one year later than basketball</strong>: Swiss Volley counts from the season's second calendar year and Swiss Basketball from its first, so the same U-number sits a year apart in the two sports. Swiss Volley also sets <strong>no lower bound</strong> — a U20 squad really does field 15-year-olds — which is why it reads "Birth year: 2008 and younger" instead of two years</li>
              <li>Visible on <strong>Basketball → Nachwuchs</strong>, on the youth cards on the <strong>Volleyball</strong> page, and on the <strong>DU23, HU23 and HU20</strong> team pages</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.18.0 — 2026-08-11</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>The website's text can now be changed by us</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The website admin has a new <strong>Page texts</strong> section: pick a page, adjust the text in German and English, save. The change is <strong>live within seconds</strong> — no detour through the code, and no waiting for the site to be rebuilt</li>
              <li>The <strong>original wording is always kept</strong>. "Original" brings it back, even months later — nothing done in the browser can overwrite the wording the site shipped with</li>
              <li><strong>Every text on the website</strong> is available, grouped by page and listed in the order it appears on that page. If you know the text but not the page, the search finds it. Header, footer and the forms' messages are their own groups</li>
              <li>What is <strong>not</strong> possible here: a link or bold text mid-sentence. Text is deliberately applied as plain text — which is exactly why an editable text cannot open a security hole</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>"Most home games" was not true</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The game scheduling page said that <strong>most home games</strong> take place on game Saturdays. That is not the case — and the claim appeared in <strong>three places</strong>: the intro text, the "Game Saturdays" section, and the Kantonsschule Wiedikon hall</li>
              <li>All three now describe game Saturdays without claiming how many games fall on them, in German and English</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.17.0 — 2026-08-08</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>The girls' youth cards had gone blank</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The <strong>U18 and U16 Mädchen cards showed no training, no coach and no status</strong> at all. The club had renamed the two girls' squads in Directus — to <strong>DU18 Spark</strong> and <strong>DU18 Fire</strong> — and the page matched teams against a fixed list of names, so after the rename nothing matched and both cards emptied themselves. It was the third rename these teams have been through, and it emptied them every time</li>
              <li>The page no longer holds a list of teams at all: it <strong>renders one card per team Directus actually has</strong>, working out the age group from the team's own name. A squad added shows up, a squad dropped disappears, and a rename carries through — without the page being edited</li>
              <li>So <strong>U18 now has both girls' squads</strong> side by side, each under its own name, and <strong>U16 has no girls' card</strong>, because this season the club has no U16 girls' team — DU18 Fire is a U18 team that plays down in the U16 league. The team grid on the Basketball page follows the same two names</li>
              <li>Where a team's name in Directus is just its age code, the German label stays: "U8 Mixed" reads better than "MU8"</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>Mixed teams can take girls and boys separately</h3>
