            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="changelog-entry">
          <div class="changelog-meta">v1.16.4 — 2026-07-30</div>
          <div class="changelog-group">
            <h3>The membership fee tables were cut off on the right</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>The three tables on <strong>Membership</strong> sat three across on a desktop, which left each column too narrow for its own content. The category descriptions could not wrap, so the tables overflowed their columns: the <strong>fee amounts were pushed out of sight</strong> behind a scrollbar, on the very page whose job is to state them</li>
              <li><strong>Volleyball and basketball now sit side by side</strong>, with the Swiss Volley licence fees below volleyball, where they belong. Two full-width columns fit their text, so nothing is clipped. On a phone the three still stack in that order</li>
